#6. A college analyzes the relationship between students’ study hours and examination marks to understand how study time is associated with academic performance. The study hours are [2, 4, 6, 8, 10], and the corresponding marks are [35, 45, 60, 75, 85]. Write a Python program to calculate the sample covariance between study hours and marks, and to draw a scatter plot showing their relationship.
import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

hours = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]
marks = [35, 45, 60, 75, 85]

print("Sample Covariance:",
      np.cov(hours, marks)[0, 1])

plt.scatter(hours, marks)
plt.xlabel("Study Hours")
plt.ylabel("Exam Marks")
plt.title("Study Hours vs Marks")
plt.grid()
plt.show()
